    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b1532a7a6c34c67be7402d20b342e45",
      "statement": "SkeletonAnimationEditor.OnDisable is protected virtual and AnnotatedAnimationClipEditor overrides it calling base, because a private declaration on both hid rather than overrode the base method, leaving Unity to dispatch only to the derived version and leaking a PreviewRenderUtility plus two Allocator.Persistent NativeArrays for every inspector opened on an annotated clip.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Editor/SkeletonAnimationEditor.cs#L33-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c62931807442ca901155620ae5d335faaccfa0ddea2851aa674bdef39c66b87:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Editor/AnnotatedAnimationClipEditor.cs#L26-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2ee0c157467b0467cd5d7369a52bf57d87f159984012f51b8a97108ded89993:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5526e8291a394dabb4ac10e5b156b506",
      "statement": "SkeletonPreview holds no playback state and exposes only a Source and a Frame, so the clip inspector's preview settings and the clip editor window's transport bar drive the same rendering code; Source is typed as the base SkeletonAnimation so FrameCount and GetFrame bind to the whole-clip members rather than AnnotatedAnimationClip's slice-local shadows.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Editor/Preview/SkeletonPreview.cs#L40-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30cbdc2768c4fd1bdcd661bf7d1daad7b76f97cee51ba4e1eef36354c220307b:"
        },
        {
